======================================================================
SUMMARY: Why LayerNorm Amplifies Position Signal
======================================================================

Key Findings:

1. VARIANCE REDISTRIBUTION:
   - Pre-LN variance-position correlation: -0.5773
   - Post-LN variance-position correlation: -0.9600
   
2. NORM vs DIRECTION vs MAGNITUDE:
   - Full activations R²: 0.7633
   - Direction only R²: 0.7537  
   - Magnitude only R²: 0.7599

3. LN GAIN/BIAS EFFECT:
   - Before gain/bias: norm-pos corr = -0.9601
   - After gain/bias: norm-pos corr = -0.9601

4. THEORETICAL FIT:
   - Expected norm ratio (1/sqrt(i+1)) correlation with actual: 0.9994

Interpretation:
- LayerNorm normalizes variance to 1, but this doesn't destroy position info
- Position is encoded in the OUTPUT NORM of LN (not input variance)
- The gain/bias parameters maintain the position signal
- Direction vs Magnitude: Magnitude dominates

